<title>TURKEY: Turkey 7th beet test shows rise to 7.31 t sugar/ha.</title>
<headline>Turkey 7th beet test shows rise to 7.31 t sugar/ha.</headline>
<dateline>ANKARA 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results of Turkey's seventh beet test, carried out on September 15, showed a rise to 7.31 tonnes of sugar per hectare from 7.07 tonnes at the same point in 1995, Turkey's state sugar refineries Turkseker said on Thursday.</p>
<p>It said average sugar content was 15.2 percent, down from 15.3 percent in the previous year's corresponding test.  </p>
<p>Turkey holds beet tests at 15-day intervals. Data for the fifth test came from 28 refineries throughout the country.</p>
<p>Details follow.</p>
<p>			     7th test 96    7th test 95    6th test 96</p>
<p>Sugar weight</p>
<p> per hectare (tonnes)     7.310	    7.070	    6.130</p>
<p>Average sugar</p>
<p> content (pct)	     15.2	     15.3	     14.7</p>
<p>Number of beets</p>
<p> per hectare		 78,570	   82,370	   78,600</p>
<p>Root weight</p>
<p> per hectare (tonnes)    47.970	   46.190	   41.640</p>
<p>Ratio of leaf</p>
<p>weight to beet weight</p>
<p> (leaf/beet)		  0.44	     0.50	     0.68</p>
<p>--Ercan Ersoy, Ankara Newsroom, 90-312-4462940</p>
</text>
